-- A3. discriminant-square analysis of the fractal family --
   D(d) = (d+2)^2 - 8.  D(d) = k^2  <=>  (d+2-k)(d+2+k) = 8,
   same-parity factor pairs of 8: only 2 x 4  =>  d+2 = 3, k = 1  =>  d = 1.
   exhaustive check d = 2..2000, square D(d): NONE
   => inside the actual class (d >= 2; d=1 is disconnected/degenerate),
      irrationality of the spectral roots is UNIVERSAL and PROVED,
      not just measured.  The binary on this side: D square <=> d=1 (out
      of class) <=> rational spectrum; D non-square <=> irrational.

==============================================================================
PART B — corridor or wallpaper: the two square-discriminant engines
==============================================================================

-- B1. wheel seam quadratics: coefficient signs across the sample --
  classes scanned: 271;  A,B,C all strictly positive: 255
  non-strict cases: 16 — ALL have C == 0 (the class's first
    seam address is 0: B[r] = 0 and L[r] = 0, i.e. small r with 2a < b).
    A,B >= 0 and C >= 0 ALWAYS; no negative coefficient ever occurs.
  violations with any negative coefficient: NONE
  negative-discriminant classes exist (complex roots): [(2, 3, 1, '-3'), (2, 7, 2, '-3'), (2, 7, 3, '-7'), (2, 7, 4, '-3'), (3, 4, 2, '-8')]

  ROOT-SIGN ARGUMENT:  N(t) counts seam addresses, so A,B >= 0, C >= 0;
  such a quadratic has NO strictly positive root (C=0 puts a root AT 0,
  the other then negative; A,B,C > 0 excludes every root >= 0).
  The fractal spectral factor x^2-(d+2)x+2 has BOTH roots strictly
  positive.  A connected graph Laplacian factor has all roots >= 0 and,
  as a factor of a singular polynomial, root 0 available; the wheel's
  positive-coefficient classes cannot supply a positive-root factor.
  Therefore no wheel seam class polynomial can BE the fractal spectral
  factor (nor any Laplacian factor with a positive root).  The two
  polynomial families are DISJOINT.  Corridor at the object level:
  CLOSED by sign, independent of any computation.

-- B2. what survives the disjointness: the shared classifier --
  Wheel: square Delta <=> factors over Q <=> identically composite.
  Fractal: D(d) square <=> d=1 (out of class) <=> rational spectrum.
  Both binaries reduce to: 'is the discriminant of an integer quadratic
  a perfect square' = Q-factorability.  That is the quadratic formula,
  genus 0, known since antiquity.  Rhyme level: shared classifier,
  not shared mechanism.  Analogy, not identity.

